<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mursili II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1321–1295 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mursili II was King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> from about 1321 to 1295 BCE, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a>. His annals record yearly campaigns against the Kaska in the north and against Azzi-Hayasa, and his conquest of Arzawa around 1320 BCE, after which he divided its lands among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> kings bound by treaties, such as those of the Seha River Land and Hapalla. He also put down revolts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, including Nuhashshe.</p></div>
